core_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.0957984166371893,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":48.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.5760248807664597,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.003004426923191472,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":41.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.14261273986349132,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":96.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.024489976515847278,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":12.8,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.2436885884027572,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.015871341710357534,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":69.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.041320096592433596,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":31.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.08218,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":54.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Farmland Partners Inc. is an internally managed real estate company that owns and seeks to acquire high-quality North American farmland and makes loans to third-party farmers (both tenant and non-tenant) and landowners secured by farm real estate and/or other agricultural related assets. As of September 30, 2026, the Company owned approximately 70,000 acres of farmland in 11 states, including Arkansas, California, Colorado, Illinois, Indiana, Louisiana, Missouri, Nebraska, South Carolina, Texas and West Virginia. In addition, the Company owns land and buildings for four agriculture equipment dealerships in Ohio leased to Ag Pro under the John Deere brand. The Company elected to be taxed as a real estate investment trust, or REIT, for U.S. federal income tax purposes, commencing with the taxable year ended December 31, 2014. Farmland Partners Inc. was established on September 27, 2013, and is based in Denver, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Luca  Fabbri | President, CEO & Board Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $839,616 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11 people. Revenue per employee of $4.7M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 26%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $196K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Farmland Partners Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $417M market cap on $52M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 24.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 4.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 43% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.43281963433251613},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 58% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (FPI) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/8/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_FPI_Edition_112126075002_1795265402.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795265402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Record FPI buying returns, but foreign investors are still picking their spots","source":"livemint.com","link":"https://www.livemint.com/market/record-fpi-buying-returns-but-foreign-investors-are-still-picking-their-spots-11795089128507.html","date":"2026-1